FG-DUCS: origins, dependency licenses, and publication status

This is a local source-package candidate. No public push or Release has been
created. All solver and third-party JARs are excluded from this repository.
fetch_assets.py obtains exact dependencies directly from the official MTSA
upstream tree, or imports an existing lawfully obtained solver copy, with size
and SHA-256 checks. Availability at an upstream URL is not redistribution
permission. The new-script MIT grant in LICENSE does not override any item below.

1. MTSA-derived sources

Upstream: https://mtsa.dc.uba.ar/
Repository: https://git.exactas.uba.ar/lafhis/mtsa
Dependency acquisition is pinned to upstream commit
 d10ba71f092dc9645a80d2752bd089691f158156
The FG-DUCS extension is in ltsa.updatingControllers.otf. Inherited Java sources,
models and third-party source headers retain their original origin and terms.
A license granting redistribution of the complete MTSA source collection has
not been established from the inspected upstream repository/site/POM.
The authors have confirmed redistribution permission for the MTSA-derived sources.
This confirmation is independent of the upstream-documentation search and
does not extend to third-party binary dependencies. The artifact therefore
includes the complete MTSA-derived tool sources with the FG-DUCS extension.

Individual source portions have separate notices: Oracle SpringUtilities,
JUNG-derived layout code, LUFA, and Arduino/Wiring code. TarjanAlgorithm contains
both a BSD-style header and an AGPLv3 header; an express choice between those
terms has not been established. No existing copyright, condition or disclaimer
is removed or replaced by the new-script license. A permissive license on a
new script is not a permissive license on this inherited collection.

The optional src/main/SPECTRATranslator subtree and src/test/benchmarks are
also retained as source/model material. SPECTRA is a separate Eclipse tool,
not part of the verified Maven build. The three component LICENSE files in
Translator, spectra-lang and spectra-synt reproduce BSD-3-Clause terms.
Two net.sf.javabdd source files additionally retain their original GNU LGPL
header and third-party copyright/contact attribution. Their referenced
COPYING file and the exact LGPL version are absent from the inherited subtree;
no blanket BSD or MIT claim is made for that collection. Those original
headers are unchanged. Native libraries, JARs, generated binary traces and
archives are omitted. A contact-only upstream benchmark note is omitted;
personal filesystem prefixes in an upstream log are anonymized only in this
copy. These are not source-code or benchmark-input changes.

2. Exact local dependencies used by the build

All ten local Maven coordinates below originate in the official MTSA tree at
maven-root/locallib and/or maven-root/mtsa/lib. They are not bundled in this repo;
fetch_assets.py downloads upstream copies into the required paths. The two
SceneBeans files have different bytes: locallib/scenebeans.jar is 193167 bytes,
whereas the Maven SceneBeans-1.0.0.jar is 221453 bytes. The script keeps them
separate. A coordinate's declared version need not be the binary's real version.

* jargs:jargs:1.0 (jargs.jar): JArgs 1.0, BSD three-clause terms. Preserve the
  copyright, conditions and disclaimer. The release ZIP contains LICENCE:
  https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/jargs/jargs/1.0/jargs-1.0.zip
* javacv:javacv:1.0 (javacv.jar): the binary is JavaCV 0.5, whose exact license
  text is GPLv2 with the Classpath Exception. The exception concerns independent
  modules; it does not remove the JavaCV source/notice obligations:
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bytedeco/javacv/0.5/LICENSE.txt
* jgraphx:jgraphx:0.1 (jgraphx.jar): the binary is JGraphX 3.3.0.1, BSD three-clause
