3. Synoptic/WESSBAS bundle, not redistributed

The 109442641-byte JAR has internal coordinate
org.fortiss.pmwt.wex:wessbas.synoptic:1.0.0. Its extension readme and five nested
JARs match the WESSBAS Synoptic fork:
https://github.com/Wessbas/synoptic
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Wessbas/synoptic/master/Licence.md
That license applies MIT terms to the project except explicitly separately
licensed libraries under lib/. It is not a MIT grant over the entire bundle.
The precise source-to-binary correspondence of this complete object and all
nested-library conditions has not been established.

The nested objects are Daikonizer.jar, daikon.jar, plume.jar,
json-simple-1.1.1.jar, and junit-4.9b2.jar. The Daikon/Plume bundles contain TMate
SVNKit COPYING terms with source-availability conditions, and additional GNU
Library GPLv2, Apache 2.0 and Hamcrest notices. A Hamcrest LICENSE inside JUnit
4.9b2 is not a license for JUnit itself. Current Daikon core terms are not being
substituted for the terms of these older composite objects. The fetched upstream
object is identified by hash in README; it is excluded from our repo and Release.

4. Frozen shaded solver: not distributed

The 698961879-byte mtsa-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar includes all 284 Synoptic classes and all
five nested JARs byte-for-byte. Removing the separate Synoptic file therefore
does not clear the shaded binary's conditions.

More decisively, FFmpeg 4.0.1 native libraries in the shaded JAR, directly checked
for several Android and Linux ABIs, contain configuration flags --enable-gpl,
--enable-version3, --enable-nonfree and --enable-openssl, and identify themselves
as "nonfree and unredistributable". The exact FFmpeg license explains that
OpenSSL is incompatible with GPLv2/v3 and that nonfree combinations can be
unredistributable:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/n4.0.1/LICENSE.md
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bytedeco/javacpp-presets/1.4.2/ffmpeg/cppbuild.sh
This frozen binary is not publicly distributed, including as a Release asset.
Its runtime bytes are kept unchanged for the ongoing measurements. The README
retains its SHA-256 and the verified clean-cache source-build procedure. The
fetch script permits verified local import; it has no Release retrieval route.
A slim CLI binary excluding the problematic dependencies is optional work after
the v2 freeze and is not part of the current artifact or its v1 requirements.

The separate original-DUCS reference JAR (672505060 bytes, SHA-256
4ab198ba14c9f0f829c36808025aefc063e2a3a0836679490179cc407e6133e5)
is a lab-maintained build of source commit
e1bf040b83e36b36308bce22e280133682986250, not an identified publication release.
Its Linux libavcodec.so.58 likewise contains nonfree/GPL/OpenSSL configuration
and identifies itself as nonfree and unredistributable. It is omitted from the
public artifact and all Releases. Only the separate adapter source, inputs,
scripts and sanitized observations are included here. The private Xeon transfer
ZIP is not part of this public source package.

