6. Privacy and required attribution

Submission-author names, affiliations, personal paths and contact details are
excluded. Required third-party legal notices are not replaced by anonymous
invented copyright holders. Existing upstream source headers are preserved.
This distinguishes attribution to upstream software from identifying the
submission authors; any actual collision requires resolution before publication.
